== Rolling stock ==

=== Current ===
* '''7000 series''' (Type D, 5-car, 2025–present) — Manufactured by [[Okami Heavy Industries]], the 7000 series is the newest rolling stock on the Chūō Line. Introduced in 2025, these trains replace the aging 3000 series linear motor trains and represent a return to conventional traction technology. The 7000 series features modern passenger amenities, improved energy efficiency, and enhanced reliability.
* '''4000 series''' (flagship, 2023–present) — Introduced in 2023 on both the Chūō and [[Miyoshi Line]]s, the 4000 series represents the flagship rolling stock of the Okami Metro network. These premium trains feature advanced design elements, state-of-the-art passenger information systems, and superior ride comfort. The deployment of the 4000 series on the Chūō Line underscores the line's importance as a central corridor.

=== Retired ===
* '''3000 series''' (legacy linear motor, 1990–2025) — Introduced in 1990, the 3000 series utilised [[linear motor]] technology, which allowed for smaller tunnel diameters and reduced construction costs. These trains served the Chūō Line for over three decades but are being progressively retired as the line transitions to the new 7000 series standard trains. The linear motor technology, while innovative for its time, proved more expensive to maintain than conventional traction systems.

